 },
 "reading": "{label}, counted at this boundary: {boundary}. About {display} for the hour. {evidence}",
 "details": [
  "The router and the device are the same on every row, so they never explain a difference between rows.",
  "The data center share of a streamed hour is unsettled: current readings run from about 0.6 to about 190 Wh at 3.5 GB an hour, with the bottom-up ones near 1 to 4 Wh. The high end is a top-down average spread over all bytes, an upper bound and not a literal share.",
  "An AI chat app drew 0.7 to 3.3 W on one iPhone, the same order as the phone here, so chat is not lighter on the device. No source measures a chat app and a video app on one phone and one network."
 ],
